Vercel Speed Insights Installation and Configuration for Next.js

SUMMARY:
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Mudra application.
The project is using Next.js 16.1.3 with App Router, and Speed Insights has been properly integrated into the root layout.

CHANGES MADE:

1. Package Installation:
   - Installed @vercel/speed-insights@^1.3.1 using pnpm
   - Updated package.json with the new dependency
   - Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with resolved dependency information

2. Code Changes:
   Modified: /app/layout.tsx
   - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
   - Added component: `<SpeedInsights />` in the body section, placed after the existing `<Analytics />` component
   - Component placement follows best practices: inside the body tag, alongside other monitoring/analytics components

IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS:

Project Configuration:
- Next.js version: 16.1.3
- Router: App Router (using /app directory)
- Package manager: pnpm
- Already had Vercel Analytics configured, making this a natural addition

Component Placement:
The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout's body element, positioned after the Analytics component. This ensures:
- The component initializes early and captures performance metrics
- It's not nested too deeply in the component tree
- It's at the same level as other first-party Vercel integrations (Analytics)

VERIFICATION:
- Package installation confirmed via package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml
- Import statements are correct for Next.js 13.5+ with App Router
- Component export path verified in node_modules
- No breaking changes to existing code
- All existing functionality preserved

NEXT STEPS FOR DEPLOYMENT:
1. Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically collect Web Vitals data
2. Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the "Speed Insights" tab
3. No additional configuration needed - the component works out of the box with Vercel deployments
4. The dsn prop can be optionally configured if using non-Vercel hosting
